{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"The reference DSO preserves helper call boundaries through its PLT, while Rust had inlined helpers into callers; that changes which NaN payload survives even when the numeric result is equivalent. I’m preventing inlining on every ABI entry point to mirror those boundaries, and reversing the multiply operand order in `c2Mulvs` to match GCC’s packed instruction operand order."}}
